### Variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000/api
@studentId = 1
# Coller ici l'accessToken retourné par /api/auth/login
@token = eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...

###
### Health Check (public)
###
GET http://localhost:3000/health

###
### === AUTHENTIFICATION (JWT) ===
###

### POST - Créer un compte (rôle STUDENT)
POST @baseUrl/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "jean.dupont@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### POST - Se connecter et récupérer un access token
POST @baseUrl/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "jean.dupont@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### GET - Utilisateur courant
GET @baseUrl/auth/whoami
Authorization: Bearer @token

### OPTIONS - Préflight CORS (ce que le navigateur envoie avant un appel protégé)
OPTIONS @baseUrl/students
Origin: http://localhost:5173
Access-Control-Request-Method: POST
Access-Control-Request-Headers: authorization,content-type

###
### === ÉTUDIANTS (token requis) ===
###

### GET - Lister tous les étudiants (authentifié)
GET @baseUrl/students
Authorization: Bearer @token

### GET - Récupérer un étudiant par ID (authentifié)
GET @baseUrl/students/@studentId
Authorization: Bearer @token

### POST - Créer un nouvel étudiant (ADMIN)
POST @baseUrl/students
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer @token

{
  "firstName": "Jean",
  "lastName": "Dupont",
  "email": "jean.dupont@example.com",
  "phone": "+33612345678",
  "dateOfBirth": "2000-01-15",
  "address": "123 Rue de Paris, 75000 Paris"
}

### POST - Créer un deuxième étudiant (ADMIN)
POST @baseUrl/students
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer @token

{
  "firstName": "Marie",
  "lastName": "Martin",
  "email": "marie.martin@example.com",
  "phone": "+33698765432",
  "dateOfBirth": "2001-05-20",
  "address": "456 Avenue des Champs, 75008 Paris"
}

### PUT - Mettre à jour complètement un étudiant (ADMIN)
PUT @baseUrl/students/@studentId
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer @token

{
  "firstName": "Jean-Paul",
  "lastName": "Bernard",
  "email": "jean.paul.bernard@example.com",
  "phone": "+33755667788",
  "dateOfBirth": "2000-01-15",
  "address": "999 Boulevard Saint-Germain, 75005 Paris"
}

### PATCH - Mettre à jour partiellement un étudiant (juste le téléphone) (ADMIN)
PATCH @baseUrl/students/@studentId
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer @token

{
  "phone": "+33622334455"
}

### PATCH - Mettre à jour partiellement un étudiant (juste l'adresse) (ADMIN)
PATCH @baseUrl/students/@studentId
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer @token

{
  "address": "555 Rue de Rivoli, 75001 Paris"
}

### DELETE - Supprimer un étudiant (ADMIN)
DELETE @baseUrl/students/@studentId
Authorization: Bearer @token

###
### Error Examples
###

### Erreur 401 - Token absent
GET @baseUrl/students

### Erreur 401 - Token invalide
GET @baseUrl/students
Authorization: Bearer abc.def.ghi

### Erreur 401 - Mauvais identifiants
POST @baseUrl/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "jean.dupont@example.com",
  "password": "wrongpassword"
}

### Erreur 403 - Rôle STUDENT sur un endpoint ADMIN
POST @baseUrl/students
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer @token

{
  "firstName": "Forbidden",
  "lastName": "User",
  "email": "forbidden@example.com"
}

### Erreur 404 - Étudiant non trouvé
GET @baseUrl/students/99999
Authorization: Bearer @token

### Erreur 400 - Email invalide
POST @baseUrl/students
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer @token

{
  "firstName": "Test",
  "lastName": "User",
  "email": "invalid-email",
  "phone": "+33612345678"
}

### Erreur 400 - Email déjà existant
POST @baseUrl/students
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer @token

{
  "firstName": "Duplicate",
  "lastName": "Email",
  "email": "jean.dupont@example.com",
  "phone": "+33612345678"
}

### Erreur 400 - Champs requis manquants
POST @baseUrl/students
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer @token

{
  "firstName": "Test",
  "lastName": "User"
}
